// "Four Ages" — Age of Empires II (Definitive Edition) rules: Dark, Feudal, Castle and Imperial Age, each reached at
// the town centre after two different buildings of the age before. Villagers gather at AoE II rates (berries ~0.31,
// wood ~0.39, gold ~0.38, stone ~0.36 a second, 10 a trip) and drop off at the town centre, mill, lumber and mining camps;
// farms hold 175 food and are rebuilt when used up. Two armors (melee / pierce): damage = attack + bonuses vs classes
// (spearmen vs cavalry, archers vs spearmen, skirmishers vs archers, rams vs buildings) - armor, at least 1. Blacksmith,
// economy and university technologies with AoE II prices. Population: houses (+5), town centre (+5), castle (+20), 200 max.
// Not yet here (engine plan): garrisoning (town centre arrows per villager, ring the bell), gates, market and trade,
// civilizations with unique units, docks, relics, formations, stances.
